// =====================================================================================
// D5 - Workload identity blocked by Conditional Access (AADSTS53003)
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Maps to  : POC Test E - CA Enforcement: Full Block Demonstration
// Table    : AADServicePrincipalSignInLogs  (diagnostic category: ServicePrincipalSignInLogs)
// Severity : 2 (Warning)
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What it finds
//   Token issuance denied to a service principal by a Conditional Access policy.
//   ResultType 53003 is the definitive "Conditional Access blocked this" code.
//
// Why it matters - two different stories, same query
//   1. CONTAINMENT WORKING. A risky identity tried to get a token and could not. The
//      block happens at the token issuance layer, so the identity gets nothing for ANY
//      resource - not Graph, not ARM, not Key Vault, not Fabric.
//   2. FALSE POSITIVE HURTING PRODUCTION. A legitimate identity got caught by the risk
//      policy and a real workload is now failing. You need to know within minutes, not
//      when the application owner opens a ticket tomorrow.
//
//   Both need eyes. That is why this alert exists even though a block is "good news".
//
// Triage
//   1. Look up the AppId in D2. Is there a genuine risk detection behind the block?
//   2. If yes: containment is working. Continue the investigation, leave it blocked.
//   3. If no, or if the risk was an admin confirmation made in error: dismiss the risk in
//      Identity Protection to restore access. No secret rotation is required if the
//      identity was not actually compromised.
// =====================================================================================

let Lookback = 24h;
AADServicePrincipalSignInLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(Lookback)
| where ResultType == 53003
| extend AppliedPolicies = tostring(ConditionalAccessPolicies)
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    ServicePrincipalName,
    ServicePrincipalId,
    AppId,
    ResourceDisplayName,
    IPAddress,
    ResultType,
    ResultDescription,
    AppliedPolicies
| order by TimeGenerated desc
